<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Freehand (Lasso) Selection</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Region &gt; Freehand</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or from the</span> <span class="Path">toolbar</span><span lang="EN-GB">. If</span> <span class="Command">Freehand Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not selected on the toolbar, hold down the left mouse button on the current selection for a second to show up the drop-down toolbar. Select</span> <span class="Button">Freehand Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button from there.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When</span> <span class="Mode">Freehand Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode is selected, press on the toolbar button to activate it.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Mouse pointer in</span> <span class="Mode">Freehand Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode<img src="../images/image270.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Then use the left mouse button to draw a free-form shape on the objects in the</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../User_Interface/Viewport.htm">viewport</a></span></u><span lang="EN-GB">. When release mouse button, selection area will be automatically closed. When use</span> <span class="Command">Freehand Selection</span><span lang="EN-GB">, all currently selected areas will be deselected.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">To add Freehand selection to the current one h</span>old down the <span class="Shortcut">Ctrl</span> key while drawing with the mouse.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">To exclude <span lang="EN-GB">Freehand</span> selection from the existing one, hold down the <span class="Shortcut">Alt</span> key while drawing with the mouse.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">T</span>he <span class="Mode">Freehand Selection</span> mode will remain active until you switch to another mode.</p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">The selection will consist of all visible points and whole visible entities that are inside. Compound entities (like scan data, meshes, point clouds, polylines, etc.) can be selected partially or wholly, depending on what amount of them is covered by the shape that is drawn. Datum points and lines must be inside in order to be selected. Centres of datum planes, datum circles, and datum spheres as well as axes of datum cylinders is enough to be inside in order to be selected.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This mode is not stored so next time when you run KUBE,</span> <span class="Mode">Polygonal Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will be selected automatically.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span class="Command">Freehand Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is mainly</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>used</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">for selecting areas with irregular shape.</span></p>
